To create a Chrome extension that saves the contents of the current webpage, you can follow these steps:

### 1. Create the Manifest File (`manifest.json`)

This file defines the structure and permissions of your extension.

```json
{
  "manifest_version": 3,
  "name": "Page Content Saver",
  "version": "1.0",
  "description": "Saves the content of the current webpage.",
  "permissions": [
    "activeTab"
  ],
  "action": {
    "default_popup": "popup.html",
    "default_icon": {
      "16": "icons/icon16.png",
      "48": "icons/icon48.png",
      "128": "icons/icon128.png"
    }
  },
  "background": {
    "service_worker": "background.js"
  }
