To generate SV (SystemVerilog) constraints ensuring that the number of transitions from the previous output is exactly 5, you can use a combination of `posedge` and `negedge` events along with counters or conditional statements. Here's an example:

```systemverilog
module testbench;
    reg clk = 0;
    reg [31:0] counter = 0;

    initial begin
        $display("Starting simulation...");
        #10; // Wait for 10 time units
        $finish;
    end

    always begin
        #10; // Generate clock signal
        clk = ~clk;
    end

    constraint transition_count {
        @(posedge clk) if (counter == 49) begin // Transition occurs after 5th posedge
            counter = 0;
            assert(counter == 5) else $error("Expected 5 transitions, but got %d", counter);
        end else if (counter < 5) begin
            counter <= counter + 1;
        end
    }
endmodule
```

In this code:
