To fix this warning, you should ensure that all modifications to `modCount` are done atomically. One way to do this is by using a `synchronized` block or method to protect the modification of `modCount`. Here's how you can modify your code:

### Option 1: Using Synchronized Block

```java
public E popFirst() {
    synchronized (this) { // Lock the entire object to ensure atomicity
        if (isEmpty()) throw new NoSuchElementException();
        E elem = array[front];
        array[front] = null; // Allow GC to work
        front = (front + 1) % array.length;
        size--;
        modCount++;
        shrinkIfNeeded();
        return elem;
    }
}

public E popLast() {
    synchronized (this) { // Lock the entire object to ensure atomicity
        if (isEmpty()) throw new NoSuchElementException();
        rear = (rear - 1 + array.length) % array.length;
        E elem = array[rear];
        array[rear] = null; // Allow GC to work
        size--;
        modCount++;
        shrinkIfNeeded();
        return elem;
    }
}
```

### Option 2: Using Synchronized Method

Alternatively, you can make the `pushFirst()`, `pushLast()`, `popFirst()`, and `popLast()` methods synchronized methods:

```java
public synchronized void pushFirst(E elem) {
    expandIfNeeded();
    front = (front - 1 + array.length) % array.length;
    array[front] = elem;
    size++;
    modCount++;
}

public synchronized void pushLast(E elem) {
    expandIfNeeded();
    array[rear] = elem;
    rear = (rear + 1) % array.length;
    size++;
    modCount++;
}

public synchronized E popFirst() {
    if (isEmpty()) throw new NoSuchElementException();
    E elem = array[front];
    array[front] = null; // Allow GC to work
    front = (front + 1) % array.length;
    size--;
    modCount++;
    shrinkIfNeeded();
    return elem;
}

public synchronized E popLast() {
    if (isEmpty()) throw new NoSuchElementException();
    rear = (rear - 1 + array.length) % array.length;
    E elem = array[rear];
    array[rear] = null; // Allow GC to work
    size--;
    modCount++;
    shrinkIfNeeded();
    return elem;
}
```

Both options will ensure that the `modCount` field is modified atomically, thus eliminating the warning. Choose the option that best fits your design preferences.

